data: {"id":"chatcmpl_13fd85fa-6af5-4c03-a5b3-2422805a6b34","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1792088372,"model":"oracle/chrono-chatgpt-pro-pool","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"Referee note — C1C1 is false as stated, rather than an open conjecture. It is nevertheless a meaningful mathematical assertion under the usual convention for nonnegative integer powers. The substantive defect is the unrestricted choice of the integer bases  $p,q$ , not merely an omitted definition.No PDF is available in this conversation: the file listing returned no attachments. This report therefore concerns the confirmed statement and its identical repetition in the source context. No additional manuscript hypotheses or proof have been inferred.Well-posedness and mathematical statusRead the indices as  $j,m\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge 0}$ , and specify  $x^0=1$ , including when  $x=0$ . With those conventions, all expressions are defined. Missing hypotheses that make an assertion false do not, by themselves, make it ill-posed.The displayed quadratic form belongs to the Fibonacci recurrence. The relevant characteristic roots are the two distinct roots of\n$$t^2-t-1=0,$$\nnot arbitrary integers. The opened source gives both the characteristic-root representation of second-order recurrence sequences and the corresponding Cassini identity. Its hypotheses retain the relationship between the recurrence and its roots. M Hikari+1C1 removes that relationship while retaining the Fibonacci-specific coefficients, the factor  $5$ , and the alternating sign. With the amplitudes  $a,b$  universally quantified, the fixed quadratic form requires the corresponding characteristic-root conditions; arbitrary integer bases do not meet them. This is a negative mathematical finding, not simply a failure to locate a reference.A natural correction would specify\n$$\\{p,q\\}\n=\n\\left\\{\n\\frac{1+\\sqrt5}{2},\n\\frac{1-\\sqrt5}{2}\n\\right\\}.$$\nThat correction must replace, not supplement, the assertion that  $p,q$  are integers. Keeping the integer restriction while imposing these root conditions would leave an empty parameter domain.Proof escape, information gain, and utilityProof correctness is not_checked: no proof was submitted. That assessment is separate from the statement-level status known_false.For C1 itself, escape is undetermined. There is no valid submitted deduction to classify, and an invalid strengthening should not receive credit as new mathematical content merely because the standard theorem does not imply it.For the root-restricted correction, the inspected baseline supports bind_only: the corrected identity is obtained from the existing Cassini formula by identifying initial values, shifting the index, and normalizing the resulting polynomial expression. That assessment concerns the correction, not the unrestricted C1. M HikariGeneral-theorem utility is unsupported for C1 as written, because its asserted universal conclusion is false. The corrected identity could serve an expository purpose, but that does not establish a new theorem or an open conjecture. Information gain is unassessed: no explicit model, readout, task, or faithful correspondence was supplied.The appropriate display revision is to distinguish a known identity with its required hypotheses from a genuinely unresolved question. The recommendation below is feedback on the mathematical statement, not a publication decision. All opened-source records are model-reported, not venue-verified.JSON{\n  \"recommendation\": \"revise\",\n  \"summary\": \"C1 is a meaningful but false universal assertion under the usual conventions for nonnegative integer powers. It drops the characteristic-root restrictions required by the Fibonacci Cassini identity. A root-restricted correction is covered by the inspected known identity, but it changes the stated domain. No PDF attachment or submitted proof was available.\",\n  \"strengths\": [\n    \"The confirmed statement is explicit enough to identify its quantifier and hypothesis defect.\",\n    \"A closely related corrected statement has a directly inspectable Cassini-identity baseline.\"\n  ],\n  \"concerns\": [\n    \"The bases p and q are quantified as arbitrary integers, although the displayed Fibonacci-specific quadratic identity requires characteristic-root restrictions.\",\n    \"Adding the two Fibonacci-root conditions while retaining p,q in Z would produce an empty parameter domain rather than a substantive repair.\",\n    \"The conventions for j and for zero to the zeroth power should be explicit.\",\n    \"The referenced PDF was not available, so no manuscript-local definitions, qualifications, or proof could be inspected.\",\n    \"Neither the false statement nor its known correction establishes new conjectural content.\"\n  ],\n  \"claims\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"C1\",\n      \"correctness\": \"not_checked\",\n      \"shape\": null,\n      \"witnesses\": [],\n      \"note\": \"Statement status, proof correctness, escape, information gain, and utility are separate. The statement-level assessment is known_false. Proof correctness remains not_checked because no proof was submitted. Escape for the exact C1 is undetermined, with no proof shape or live witnesses; the natural root-restricted correction is bind_only relative to the opened baseline. General-theorem utility is unsupported for the false assertion. Information gain is null. No named open-problem settlement is claimed.\",\n      \"conjecture\": {\n        \"well_posed\": true,\n        \"well_posed_reason\": \"Under the natural reading j,m in Z_{\\u22650} and the algebraic convention x^0=1, including 0^0=1, u_j and both sides of the equality are defined for every quantified input. These conventions should be stated. The missing characteristic-root restrictions are a truth-condition defect, not merely a definitional ambiguity.\",\n        \"status\": \"known_false\",\n        \"status_reason\": \"The universal identity is false for arbitrary integer exponential bases. Its fixed quadratic form is associated with the characteristic polynomial t^2-t-1. Universal freedom in the amplitudes a,b requires the corresponding root conditions, which arbitrary integer p,q do not satisfy. The opened Cassini baseline supplies a related identity with recurrence hypotheses; it does not license dropping those hypotheses. This is an elementary statement-level diagnosis, not a claim that a published refutation of this exact wording was located.\",\n        \"named_works\": [\n          \"On Some Properties of Horadam Polynomials [opened: https://www.m-hikari.com/imf-password2009/25-28-2009/kocerIMF25-28-2009.pdf]\"\n        ],\n        \"known\": [\n          \"On Some Properties of Horadam Polynomials [opened: https://www.m-hikari.com/imf-password2009/25-28-2009/kocerIMF25-28-2009.pdf]\"\n        ],\n        \"escape\": \"undetermined\",\n        \"escape_reason\": \"For the exact false C1, no valid proof is supplied or identified, so there is no justified content or bind_only classification of a deduction. This is not evidence of novelty. The distinct-Fibonacci-root correction is separately bind_only by specialization and polynomial normalization of the opened Cassini identity.\",\n        \"suggestions\": [\n          \"For a known-identity display, replace the arbitrary integer-base quantifier by the explicit unordered pair {(1+sqrt(5))/2,(1-sqrt(5))/2}, retaining the desired amplitude domain and nonnegative integer indices.\",\n          \"Alternatively, formulate the statement directly for a sequence satisfying the Fibonacci recurrence, with its invariant expressed in terms of the specified initial values.\",\n          \"State j,m in Z_{\\u22650} and the convention for exponent zero. Do not present the unrestricted C1, or a known root-restricted correction, as an established open conjecture.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"methodology\": {\n        \"baseline\": [\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"The supplied claim quantifies p,q,a,b as integers and m as a nonnegative integer, defines u_j=a p^j+b q^j, and asserts the displayed equality. It supplies no characteristic-root equations, distinctness condition, or recurrence hypothesis.\",\n            \"location\": \"Confirmed Statements, C1.statement; repeated in Source Context, sole mathematical sentence. No PDF manuscript location is available.\",\n            \"source\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"For h_1=A, h_2=B and h_{n+1}=h_n+h_{n-1}, the Cassini specialization i"},"finish_reason":null}]}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl_13fd85fa-6af5-4c03-a5b3-2422805a6b34","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1792088372,"model":"oracle/chrono-chatgpt-pro-pool","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"s h_n^2-h_{n+1}h_{n-1}=(-1)^(n-2)(B^2-AB-A^2), for n\u003e=2 and real initial values A,B.\",\n            \"location\": \"Section 2.1, equations (10)-(11), printed page 1245; Corollary 5, equation (20), printed page 1250, specialized to x=p=q=1 using the polynomial sequence's h_1,h_2 indexing.\",\n            \"source\": \"On Some Properties of Horadam Polynomials [opened: https://www.m-hikari.com/imf-password2009/25-28-2009/kocerIMF25-28-2009.pdf]\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"searched\": [\n          \"Conversation-file metadata listing: no attachments were present.\",\n          \"General web search queries: generalized Cassini identity Horadam sequence Binet roots; \\\"Cassini\\\" \\\"p+q\\\" \\\"roots\\\" identity.\",\n          \"Additional web queries: Horadam \\\"Basic properties\\\" \\\"1965\\\" pdf; \\\"Cassini\\\" \\\"a\\\" \\\"b\\\" \\\"arbitrary\\\" \\\"roots\\\" Fibonacci identity; \\\"Basic properties of a certain generalized sequence\\\" site:fq.math.ca.\",\n          \"Additional targeted queries: \\\"Cassini\\\" \\\"A\\\" \\\"B\\\" \\\"5AB\\\"; \\\"Cassini\\\" \\\"arbitrary\\\" \\\"p\\\" \\\"q\\\" \\\"a\\\" \\\"b\\\" \\\"identity\\\". Unopened search hits were not treated as mathematical evidence.\",\n          \"Inspected the publisher-hosted PDF of On Some Properties of Horadam Polynomials, including its recurrence definitions, characteristic-root formulas, and Corollary 5. Relevant printed pages 1243, 1244, and 1250 were also inspected as page images.\",\n          \"Opened the Fibonacci Quarterly volume 3, number 3 contents page. Attempts to retrieve two earlier full-text articles failed; their theorem contents were excluded.\",\n          \"Search scope: second-order recurrence sequences, characteristic-root representations, and Cassini identities relevant to C1. No direct MathSciNet or zbMATH database search and no exhaustive literature search were performed.\"\n        ],\n        \"literature\": \"supported\",\n        \"binding_analysis\": \"Set h_{j+1}=u_j, A=a+b, B=ap+bq, and n=m+2. When p,q are the two distinct Fibonacci roots, the recurrence hypothesis is met and polynomial normalization gives B^2-AB-A^2=-5ab. This yields the corrected identity by binding. C1 supplies neither the necessary root hypotheses nor a compatible root domain. Renaming, projection, recombination, and assumption substitution cannot remove unmet hypotheses.\",\n        \"delta\": \"The exact additional obligation in C1 is to retain the same quadratic coefficients and the factor -5ab(-1)^m uniformly for every integer p,q,a,b and nonnegative integer m, without characteristic-root or recurrence restrictions. That unrestricted obligation is false. No alternative non-binding construction, bound, or valid strengthened proposition has been supplied. Restoring the distinct Fibonacci roots removes this purported extension and returns to the known specialization.\",\n        \"escape\": \"undetermined\",\n        \"witnesses\": [],\n        \"utility\": {\n          \"kind\": \"general_theorem\",\n          \"status\": \"unsupported\",\n          \"rationale\": \"An unrestricted theorem of the proposed form cannot provide the claimed utility because its conclusion is false. Pure mathematics requires no artificial downstream application, but a valid mathematical assertion is still required. The known root-restricted correction may have expository usefulness; it is not established new research progress by this submission.\",\n          \"problem\": \"Determine whether C1's displayed Cassini-type equality holds for every integer p,q,a,b and every nonnegative integer m.\",\n          \"progress\": \"The statement-level assessment is negative. A related corrected statement is covered by an opened Cassini baseline, but the submission contains no proof or new theorem.\",\n          \"prerequisites\": \"C1 provides only its parameter domains and exponential-sequence definition. The baseline comparison additionally requires the Fibonacci recurrence, supplied by the two distinct Fibonacci characteristic roots.\",\n          \"discharge\": \"The sequence definition is supplied, subject to an explicit exponent-zero convention. The additional recurrence and root hypotheses are not supplied and cannot be identified with the stipulated arbitrary integer bases. No submitted proof discharges the unrestricted obligation.\"\n        },\n        \"settlement\": null,\n        \"information_gain\": null,\n        \"limits\": [\n          \"The literature-supported comparison is limited to the inspected Cassini baseline and the root-restricted correction; it is not an exhaustive novelty or historical-priority finding.\",\n          \"No PDF attachment was available. Local prerequisite locations therefore refer only to the confirmed text, not invented manuscript pages.\",\n          \"No proof of C1 was submitted or reviewed. There is no proof shape, live proof-escape witness, or formal verification.\",\n          \"The source's polynomial indexing was used explicitly with n\u003e=2; its differently indexed discussion of Horadam numbers was not silently substituted.\",\n          \"Failed earlier full-text retrievals are not_checkable and are not premises of the report.\",\n          \"No compiled Trureturing registration, Lean verification, AURIC/FIB measurement, escape percentage, or combined score is claimed.\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"limits\": [\n    \"Only the confirmed inline assertion was available; the requested PDF could not be inspected because the conversation contained no attachments.\",\n    \"The known_false status is a statement-level mathematical assessment. The correctness field concerns an absent submitted proof and therefore remains not_checked.\",\n    \"All opened-source strings are model-reported references, never venue-verified references.\",\n    \"Earlier PDF retrievals failed at https://www.mathstat.dal.ca/FQ/Scanned/3-3/horadam.pdf, https://www.fq.math.ca/Scanned/3-3/horadam.pdf, and https://www.fq.math.ca/Scanned/5-5/horadam.pdf. Their mathematical contents are not_checkable and were not used.\",\n    \"The search was targeted rather than exhaustive. It establishes the stated baseline comparison, not a universal claim about the literature.\",\n    \"No named open-problem settlement was claimed, so settlement is null. No information-gain model or evidence was supplied, so information_gain is null.\",\n    \"The recommendation is feedback on mathematical display wording and does not decide publication.\"\n  ],\n  \"text\": \"Revise the display to separate the false unrestricted assertion from the known identity with its characteristic-root hypotheses. A repaired known identity should be presented as such, not as an unresolved conjecture. The missing PDF limits manuscript assessment; it does not remove the mathematical defect in the confirmed C1.\"\n}"},"finish_reason":null}]}

